dash: a live segment that is not there yet is waited for, not passed over

At the live edge the reader asked for the segment after the last one it
had read whether or not the manifest listed it yet. With a timeline, a
segment that is not listed is not made: the server answers 404, the
reader says "Failed to open fragment of playlist", counts on to the next
number and asks for that, which is not there either. Within a few
milliseconds it had run through hundreds of numbers, the playback had
nothing more to read, and the stream had to be opened again, which
began it once more at the start of the manifest's window. A reader
starts a minute behind the end of a timeline, or at its start when it
lists less, and one whose caller reads ahead comes to the edge.

A segment the manifest does not list, or that the clock says is not
made yet (a template without a timeline), is now waited for: half a
segment at a time, as the HLS reader waits half a target duration
between reloads, with the manifest read again between the waits where
it is the manifest that lists the segments. The wait ends with the
interrupt callback, and gives up after max_reload reloads, the option
that already bounds the reloads of a segment list.

--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c	2026-11-15 20:48:48
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c	2026-11-15 20:48:48
@@ -1653,6 +1653,22 @@
     return ret;
 }
 
+/* How long to wait before a live manifest is read again for a segment it
+ * does not list yet: half a segment, as a playlist's reader waits half a
+ * target duration, and no less than a tenth of a second. */
+static int64_t segment_wait(const struct representation *pls)
+{
+    int64_t duration = 0;
+
+    if (pls->n_timelines > 0)
+        duration = pls->timelines[pls->n_timelines - 1]->duration;
+    else
+        duration = pls->fragment_duration;
+    if (duration <= 0 || pls->fragment_timescale <= 0)
+        return AV_TIME_BASE;
+    return FFMAX(AV_TIME_BASE / 10, av_rescale(duration, AV_TIME_BASE, 2 * pls->fragment_timescale));
+}
+
 static struct fragment *get_current_fragment(struct representation *pls)
 {
     int64_t min_seq_no = 0;
@@ -1702,6 +1718,29 @@
